Z||000003||stimpy||12-31-2000||01:24 AM||||Right on Alex! Looking great! You guys have been keeping yourselves busy I must say. Now, paint that sucker oxidized gold and it could be the twin of my car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  So when is it going to be able to make its debut at the Fiero Club meet? I can't wait to see the faces on some of those know-it-alls driving the raggedy ass, haven't done a thing to their sorry ride in years POS's. HAHA!<P>You rock! <P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex2004||12-31-2000||02:15 PM||||He hit the deer probably about 55 mph or so, he was going about 70 and he seen it and coasted and then it jumped out, he slammed on the brakes and hit it, he drug it for about 30 feet or so because the roads were wet, it was caught on the headlight HAHA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. And then he got out, looked at the car, and came home, he didn't worrie about the deer, he was too pissed. the estimate was about $1800 or so, he fixed it his self though, he got the front clip off another T/A. It came about 2 inches from hitting the uni-body...eekkk... There weren't any parts left on the road except maybe a turn signal, he took the headlight out. So that is what happened.||||reg||13
